 "analyst": "Jash (JJ) Rajgandhi",
 "thesis": "Cheniere is the largest U.S. LNG exporter, and most of its Sabine Pass and Corpus Christi capacity is sold under long-term fixed-fee contracts, so cash flow depends far more on volumes than on commodity prices. Our blended $316 target (40% perpetuity DCF, 40% exit-multiple DCF, 20% trading comps) points to upside as the Corpus Christi Stage 3 trains ramp volumes, while buybacks of more than $10B authorized through 2030 and a 10%-a-year dividend growth commitment return the excess cash.",
 "catalysts": [
  "Corpus Christi Stage 3 trains reaching substantial completion and lifting volumes",
  "FID on Sabine Pass Expansion Phase 1 (bull case adds terminal EBITDA)",
  "Continued buybacks under the >$10B authorization through 2030"
 ],
 "risks": [
  "Fixed liquefaction fee / margin compression on uncontracted volumes",
  "Construction delays or cost overruns on expansion projects",
